    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While you're likely not overthinking things, these symptoms could be a sign of DVT, a clot in the deep veins of the leg, and anything above that can indeed be too risky. ADVT can make the pain worse upon movement and can have serious or even fatal repercussions if not treated early. It's essential that you at least see a professional for a thorough assessment.\n\nWest and long flight is a common place where blood clots triple their risk. I know you're not at her door right now, but it's probably best to already have her account in your file with another number just in case. DVT can and does occur individually, and the american heart association says half the time there's nothing wrong and it's a no-op to a doctor. The other half the time people die, so no risk is always too much. I'd be happy to ALTO get you to a physician, because this (womoutputs_30-33) gave me a bad hug from both DVT and COPD- unrelated Raspharitis on the way in. If you don't want to JUST see a doctor, then the cart will hit you as soon as you release it.  Or settle into Roa's… All but Dick's!\n\nAlerting Dick at",
